title ALES156 — Lotus's stereo_gate: the noise gate carried into stereo, ONE LINKED DETECTOR, the image the gate refuses to tear — opens the whole stereo dynamics family
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Chose the next crux from the whole road, not just the next ascending mono rung. The waveshaping and silence/analysis families are now whole in stereo (131-155), yet the entire DYNAMICS family (gate, compressor, limiter, expander, ALES49-51 + envelope kin) has NO stereo twin at all — the largest Lindy-durable gap left, since every mixing chain leans on dynamics and a Lotus master cannot be finished without them. So this rung opens that family on its simplest, most self-contained member: the noise gate (ALES51), memoryless, one threshold and one ratio, no attack/hold/release state.
think Gate is crux-first for the family because it names, in the plainest form, the one decision no waveshaper ever faced and every stereo dynamics processor must make: LINKED or INDEPENDENT detection. Running the mono gate twice (each channel deciding on its own magnitude) would gate the quiet right while the loud left plays — the image lurches and chatters. This is the dynamics-class twin of the bug ALES129 (stereo_normalize) named for the amplitude class: independent processing tears the inter-channel difference that IS the stereo image. So this rung LINKS the detector — decides open-or-closed once, from both channels together (key = max(|L|,|R|)), and applies that one decision to both.
think The linked law has a clean statement: a pair is gated iff BOTH channels fall below the threshold (max < thr). Because key is the MAX, when the gate closes both |L| and |R| are genuinely below threshold, so gating each reduces exactly to ALES51's mono gate on each (the below-both law, proven against the mono tool directly). When the gate opens (key >= thr) BOTH pass byte for byte, the quiet channel included — that is where linked and independent part ways, and the witness proves the difference by running the mono gate on the quiet right alone and showing it WOULD have gated it (100/80/120 -> 25/20/30 at 4:1) where stereo_gate leaves it whole.
think StereoGateError = ALES51's GateError (BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadRange) reused whole; the linked lift adds no fault. Five laws witnessed first-try GREEN: linked-detector (loud-left/quiet-right pair leaves both untouched, independent lift shown to differ), below-both (=ALES51 mono on each byte for byte, 4:1 by hand), image/sign (no magnitude expands, no sign flips, out-of-phase quiet pair returns still exactly out of phase, loud pair passes whole), knob laws (above the identity, unit ratio the identity everywhere, higher ratio monotone, huge ratio silences a closed pair), balance/atomicity/degenerate (length held, all four refusals leave both channels untouched and balanced, count 0 the identity).
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, two bounded i16 Clips, values only, one comparison of the linked key and at most one divide per channel per sample, memoryless, a self-approved design round. First-try witness GREEN, TAME bans clean, no red. Recorded lesson: for the stereo DYNAMICS class the crux is neither the silence family's joint-length lockstep nor the value-map family's image-behaviour (ALES155) — it is the LINKED DETECTOR: the open/closed decision must be shared across channels (key = max of magnitudes) or the image tears, and once gate proves the linked-detector law the compressor/limiter/expander reuse it. This is the dynamics twin of ALES129's linked-gain insight for amplitude. Front doors lotus/README.md and session-logs/README.md synced in the same commit.
loom witness=ales_stereo_gate_witness result=GREEN laws=linked-detector+below-both+image-sign+knobs+balance channels=2 class=stereo-dynamics-first-rung detector=linked-max(|L|,|R|) gate-iff=both-below-threshold cases=linked(loud-left2000/quiet-right100-both-untouched,mono-on-right-alone-differs:100/80/120->25/20/30)+below-both(=ALES51-mono-each,4:1-by-hand)+image-sign(no-expand,no-flip,out-of-phase-quiet-stays-out-of-phase,loud-pair-whole)+knobs(above-identity,unit-ratio-identity,higher-monotone,huge-silences)+balance/atomicity(4-refusals-untouched-balanced,count0-identity) reds=0
file lotus/stereo_gate.rye ALES156 — stereo_gate, the noise gate lifted to stereo by the LINKED detector: key = max(|left|,|right|) per pair decides open-or-closed once for both channels; open passes both byte for byte, closed divides each channel's own magnitude by the ratio (reducing to ALES51's mono gate on each); StereoGateError = ALES51's GateError reused whole; opens the whole stereo dynamics family.
file tools/ales_stereo_gate_witness.rish the witness — three-say (Language/Style/Lens), builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN ales-stereo-gate line.
file active-designing/20260815-061957_fill-ales156-lotus-stereo-gate.md the self-approved design read — the next crux honestly chosen (the dynamics gap), the linked-detector shape, the five laws.
file lotus/README.md front door synced — ALES156 stereo_gate (linked detector) token appended to the Status line.
file session-logs/README.md index row prepended, newest first.
recommend keep-going the stereo dynamics family grows from here; the next crux is ALES50's compressor carried into stereo (stereo_compress) reusing this rung's linked-detector law — the detector keys on max(|L|,|R|) and applies one shared gain-reduction to both so the image holds — agent-doable, no gate reached, witness GREEN, TAME clean.
